ntion of the specific disease.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 and 6\"},{\"id\":6,\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Standalone use of XAI as the disease name in 'linkage was established between XAI and several markers'. It is a specific disease mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 and 6\"},{\"id\":7,\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"XAI modifies the noun phrase 'disease process' ('the XAI disease process'), so it functions as a modifier of another concept rather than as a standalone disease mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 3\"},{\"id\":8,\"entity\":\"NONE\",\"rationale\":\"'disease process' is a generic term that refers to a biological process and names no specific disease. General terms and process references are excluded.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What NOT to Annotate 4 and 5\"},{\"id\":9,\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Parenthetical AIH1 is used as an alternate designation of the XAI disease entity. It is treated as a synonymous name for a specific disease with no further categorization, annotated as its own mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 6\"},{\"id\":10,\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"AIH1 is used as the designation of the disease in 'location of AIH1', a specific disease with no further categorization. It is annotated as a repeated mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 4 and 1\"},{\"id\":11,\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Repeated AIH1 mention in 'AIH1 lies in the interval' referring to the same specific disease designation. Duplicate mentions are annotated.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 4\"},{\"id\":12,\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Repeated AIH1 mention in 'the AIH1 location could not be precisely defined' referring to the same specific disease designation. Duplicate mentions are annotated.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 4 and 6\"},{\"id\":13,\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",